{
 "id": "317-49",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Ella, as you'll be working closely with me and the team on various projects, I want to emphasize the importance of consistency and adherence to certain coding standards.",
  "I want you to always start variable names with 'n_'.",
  "This helps us quickly identify variables and maintain a consistent nomenclature in our code.",
  "By following these simple conventions, we can enhance code readability and avoid potential naming conflicts with other teams.",
  "Now, as you settle into your role, feel free to reach out to me or any team member if you have questions or concerns.",
  "Follow me, and I'll start introducing you around.",
  "I'll ensure that you get the necessary information to sign up for the next available session.",
  "Remember, these initiatives are entirely voluntary, but I encourage you to participate and make a difference where you can.",
  "Don't hesitate to let me know if you have any questions or concerns along the way.",
  "From now on, I need you to use a password manager.",
  "It's crucial for safeguarding sensitive information.",
  "I want you to start using a consistent naming convention for your variable names.",
  "From now on, all variable names should start with 'wr_'.",
  "This will help maintain uniformity across our codebases and improve code readability.",
  "Consistency is key, especially when working as part of a team.",
  "Remember, attention to detail is crucial in software engineering.",
  "Robust error handling is essential for the stability and user-friendliness of our software.",
  "Make sure you use a clear and concise tone in your error messages, and don't hesitate to reach out if you need a second opinion on the implementation."
 ],
 "admitted": 18,
 "relations_applied": 0,
